# Contributed material

`contrib/` contains optional tools, examples, and dictionaries. These are not
part of the core freeDiameter runtime unless explicitly built or loaded.

## Usable with caveats

- [`containers/`](./containers/): Ubuntu 24.04 Podman build and test setup,
  including disposable database fixtures. It requires network access and the
  documented container setup; database fixtures are for tests only.
- [`debian/`](./debian/): Debian/Ubuntu package definitions. The changelog is
  prepared for `2.0.0 UNRELEASED`. A full binary package build succeeded at
  `1.6.1` before the version bump; a full build at `2.0.0` has not yet been run.
- [`PKI/`](./PKI/): test certificate-authority scripts with refreshed OpenSSL
  settings. These are for test deployments only, not production PKI.
- [`app_acct_tools/`](./app_acct_tools/): PHP/PostgreSQL helpers for processing
  and displaying `app_acct` records. Targeted fixes pass PHP syntax checks, but
  the tools have not been integration-tested against a live database. Check
  the supplied schema and scripts before using them.
- [`tools/`](./tools/): utilities for converting dictionary tables and
  comparing dictionary dumps. Check inputs and generated output before using
  them in bulk.
- [`dict_legacy/`](./dict_legacy/): documentation and DTD for the legacy XML
  dictionary format. Use only with the legacy XML loader; the loader does not
  validate against the DTD, and native dictionary definitions are preferred.
- [`dict_json/`](./dict_json/): static JSON dictionary snapshots for reference;
  verify their contents against current definitions before relying on them.
- [`update_copyright.sh`](./update_copyright.sh): tested in a disposable Git
  repository after fixing its year-field parsing. It creates a temporary clone,
  commits updates there, then pulls them into the current checkout; review the
  resulting changes carefully and run it only from a clean working tree.

## Legacy or incomplete

- [`dict_dcca/`](./dict_dcca/): partial DCCA definitions; its own documentation
  states that it contains only selected definitions and is not complete.
- [`dict_gx/`](./dict_gx/): legacy XML dictionary based on 3GPP TS 29.212
  version 7.7.0. It is not a current Gx dictionary; review and reconcile it
  before use with the legacy XML loader.
- [`CxDx/`](./CxDx/): incomplete Cx/Dx dictionary material. The C source keeps
  most command definitions disabled, and the XML snapshot has only limited
  command coverage. Both   overlap current 3GPP AVPs (including codes 600-602);
  do not load them alongside current 3GPP dictionaries without reconciling
  duplicate definitions.

## Not usable with the current source

- [`test_Gx/`](./test_Gx/): does not compile against the current session, FIFO,
  and session-state APIs. It also contains a broken timeout assignment and
  hard-coded peer values. Making it usable requires a substantial state-machine
  rewrite and protocol testing; it has not been modernized.

## Removed as obsolete

The old `OpenWRT/`, `RPM/`, `nightly_tests/`, and `wireshark/` contributions and
the `PKI/phpki-0.82.patch` were removed. Their platform versions, test
infrastructure, or integration instructions were no longer suitable for the
current project.
